WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.100
At this rose garden
that overlooks the ocean,

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:07.200
we meet Mr. Sanada, who can see
Death Spirits just like Mitsuki can!

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:11.100
Mr. Sanada is a gentle man who
seems to have accepted his destiny.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.740
And on his fated day, Mitsuki
has a heart to heart with him

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:16.600
just as his soul
is being collected.

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:19.270
I wonder how she felt back there.

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:22.970
So, I wonder what's
going to happen today...

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:28.740
Got that?

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:29.800
Yes.

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:42.740
What?

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.200
Everyone?

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:52.940
Ms. Oshige? Dr. Wakaoji?

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.800
Takuto? Meroko?

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:03.570
Why?

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:05.700
The reason's simple.

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:10.400
You're going to die soon.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:33.900
It was a dream?

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:36.670
What's wrong?

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:39.840
It's still night.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.770
It's nothing.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:44.840
I'm okay.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:02.470
Hey, Mitsuki.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.200
Mitsuki?

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:09.870
Ow, ow...
What're you doing?

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:14.070
I've been calling you many times,
but you act like you don't notice.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.170
Ta-dah. Look at this.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:19.840
Orientation for advancement
into junior high school?

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:24.540
Yeah. We're finally going to be
junior high school students next spring.

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:27.440
Next...spring...

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:33.000
The school uniforms we've longed for.
Wonderful upperclassmen...

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:37.340
Let me tell you though, the studies are
going to be tough in our junior high school.

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:40.040
Why did you say such
a pessimistic thing?

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:43.900
Say, Mitsuki. How about joining
the Judo club with me in junior high?

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:45.840
A manga study club
would be nice too.

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:48.840
Wait, we need to ask Mitsuki
what she wants to do.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.370
That's right.
What do you want to do?

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:54.170
You haven't decided, yet?

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:56.300
N-No. Not yet.

00:04:56.770 --> 00:05:00.370
I see. Then take your time
and think about it. Okay?

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.400
O-Okay.

00:05:02.470 --> 00:05:05.840
By next spring, that girl will...

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:14.600
Grandma, may I come in?

00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:20.240
What do you want, Mitsuki?

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:22.470
Oh... Umm... I...

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:26.500
It's nothing.

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:29.440
Good night then.

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:40.470
Jeez, what's with that attitude?!
She makes me mad!

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:42.840
Whoa. C-Calm down, Meroko!

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:44.040
I'm calm!

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:45.340
How is this calm?!

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:59.540
Since I won't be able to talk with
Grandma after next spring,

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:03.740
I wanted to reconcile with her
while I had the chance, but...

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:08.740
I failed!

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:15.870
<i>Mitsuki...</i>

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:20.340
Good morning.

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:22.140
- Good morning!
- Good morning!

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:24.700
Oh, Ms. Oshige!

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:27.770
Excuse me,
do you have a moment?

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:28.600
Sure.

00:06:29.170 --> 00:06:30.170
You go on ahead.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:31.200
Okay.

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:55.840
<i>You're going to die soon.</i>

00:06:57.840 --> 00:06:59.070
<i>You're going to die.</i>

00:07:02.340 --> 00:07:03.000
Mitsuki!

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:05.900
Are you okay?

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:15.100
Umm... Umm... I...

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:19.600
THE GREEN TOWN
"Summer Vacation Special Drama."

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:21.400
Half a year from now, huh?

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:25.470
Her health is an issue,
so I have to consult with everyone.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:27.570
If you're scared, say so.

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:29.600
Takuto...

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:33.800
Mitsuki, it's okay to say
you're scared if you're scared.

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:37.600
Because wanting to live
is human instinct.

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:38.600
Huh?

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:48.570
Th-Thanks, Takuto.
But I'm fine.

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:50.640
Fine?

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:52.970
I'm really fine!

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:56.440
Hey, I'm going to change,
so go outside.

00:08:01.970 --> 00:08:05.440
What're you thinking,
saying such a thing, Takuto?

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:10.000
It's good that she isn't
as scared as I thought.

00:08:10.470 --> 00:08:13.740
But what would you have done
if she said she was scared?

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:16.100
There's nothing we can do.

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:19.470
Do you really think
she's not scared?

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:20.500
What?

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:24.240
She's scared.
She's gotten scared!

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:31.540
Of course she is.
She's still 12 years old!

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:37.340
But even so,
she's working as hard as she can.

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:38.800
Takuto...

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:41.540
She tries really hard...
to say she's not.

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:47.070
She's saying she's fine,
so isn't that okay?

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:52.770
I don't care about Mitsuki's feelings
in the first place.

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:53.640
Meroko...

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:57.340
This is why I didn't want to
get chummy with a child.

00:08:57.670 --> 00:08:59.870
It just makes the job painful.

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:02.040
Are you being serious?!

00:09:02.570 --> 00:09:05.670
A-Anyway,
I don't want to do this anymore!

00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:06.540
Meroko!

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:11.500
Dammit!

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:15.440
How complicated.

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:18.100
They're on bad terms.

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:19.600
That's perfect.

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:22.670
With this, there will be more
chances to get close to Mero.

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:25.700
She's too good for Takuto.

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:30.070
But you snubbed her
when she hit on you!

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:35.370
Let me out! It's dark!

00:09:38.770 --> 00:09:40.170
Good work today!

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:41.640
- Good work today!
- Good work today!

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:43.170
Yes.

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:48.540
Yes. Of course we're happy to accept.
We look forward to working with you.

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:50.900
What were you talking about?

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:53.140
I accepted a drama job for you.

00:09:53.540 --> 00:09:54.200
Drama?

00:09:54.670 --> 00:09:56.640
It's a good offer.

00:09:57.000 --> 00:10:00.470
It's half a year from now,
but they're saying you'll be the star

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:03.440
and your third single will be
the main theme song.

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:05.440
Half a year from now...

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:06.970
It'll be okay!

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:09.170
I'll find a way to make it happen,
no matter what.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:15.670
You'll be in a drama,
make the song a hit,

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:19.300
and we'll do our best together half a year
from now, a year from now, and forever!

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:21.600
Okay, Mitsuki?

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:24.070
Ms. Oshige...

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:27.240
I'm home.

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:29.000
Welcome home.

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:35.370
A friend of yours delivered this while
you were out with Ms. Oshige.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:36.070
What?

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:40.240
It's about the club activities
we were talking about yesterday.

00:10:40.900 --> 00:10:46.140
<i>I'm sorry I asked you to join the Judo club</i>
<i>with me without thinking about your health.</i>

00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:51.200
<i>We asked the teacher, and there are</i>
<i>lots of activities that you can do too.</i>

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:57.100
<i>We're writing them down here in hopes</i>
<i>that there'll be an activity you want to do.</i>

00:10:57.640 --> 00:11:01.640
<i>Personally, I think you should</i>
<i>do the manga study club.</i>

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:04.470
Jeez, you guys!

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:23.970
I wonder if I was too hard on Takuto.
I guess I should head back.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:30.400
I-Izumi?!

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:33.440
W-What did you come here for?!

00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:37.070
You'd know if I said I'd only
come to the human world

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:39.300
for one reason other
than work, right?

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:41.570
Stop it!

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:44.900
You used to follow me
around so much.

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:48.570
That was then, this is now.
I think nothing of you now!

00:11:48.940 --> 00:11:51.070
I'm dedicated to Takuto now!

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:54.400
Do you like Takuto that much?

00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:58.940
Takuto's heart has
been stolen by Mitsuki.

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:06.840
A-Anyway, just go on home already!

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:20.900
You're the best, Mero.
You're really the best!

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:37.440
Mitsuki, where are you going?

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:39.440
It's almost time for dinner.

00:12:39.770 --> 00:12:42.770
Y-Yeah, Dr. Wakaoji called me in.

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:44.470
Anyway, I'll be back.

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:45.970
Mitsuki!

00:12:49.570 --> 00:12:51.570
What's all the ruckus?

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:56.370
Oh, Mitsuki said she was called in
by Dr. Wakaoji. Umm...

00:12:57.600 --> 00:12:58.600
Leave her be.

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:06.870
Don't rush so fast.
You'll trip and fall!

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:08.100
But...

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:11.500
Mitsuki!

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:13.470
Dr. Wakaoji.

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:23.770
What's everyone all flustered about?
What the heck is going on?

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:25.000
Well...

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:28.740
Is that true?
I got an email from Eichi?

00:13:28.970 --> 00:13:32.770
It's true. An email was sent to
the Full Moon official homepage.

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:34.270
Here, look.

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:41.040
I was surprised when
I heard the song.

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:44.470
Mitsuki, you made your dream
of becoming a singer come true.

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:47.740
I'm doing my best in America
to make my dream

00:13:47.770 --> 00:13:50.370
of becoming an astronomer
come true.

00:13:50.770 --> 00:13:51.770
From Eichi.

00:13:52.300 --> 00:13:55.970
It was sent with a free email address,
so we don't know where he is.

00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:58.940
But now we can get a lead
as to where he is.

00:13:59.870 --> 00:14:01.870
I can't believe it.

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:13.100
Eichi...

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:16.870
You should ask him when
he's coming back to Japan.

00:14:17.300 --> 00:14:17.970
Right!

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:22.600
All right! With this,
Mitsuki's dream will come true.

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:25.670
And what's more,
it'll be just the two of us.

00:14:25.700 --> 00:14:27.070
We'll be madly in love!

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:42.100
Oh, Takuto...

00:14:46.600 --> 00:14:49.400
To think that even the color of
the sun would look different

00:14:49.440 --> 00:14:52.970
just by getting
an email from Eichi.

00:14:56.670 --> 00:14:57.800
It's a wonder.

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:00.340
More, please.

00:15:01.370 --> 00:15:05.500
Oh, again? You've got quite
an appetite this morning.

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:09.440
I got up kind of early,
so I got hungry.

00:15:13.570 --> 00:15:14.670
This is a surprise.

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:18.270
Am I getting worse?

00:15:18.340 --> 00:15:21.240
No, just the opposite.
You've gotten a lot better.

00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:23.570
That's the Eichi effect.

00:15:23.970 --> 00:15:25.240
The Eichi effect?

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:28.640
It seems there are many cases
of incurable diseases

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:32.200
being cured by strengthened immunity
due to being happy and laughing.

00:15:32.770 --> 00:15:36.640
I'm a doctor, and I've been put to shame.
I surrender to Eichi.

00:15:41.740 --> 00:15:43.340
Strange.

00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:45.300
Even though it looks like
her sickness is going to be cured,

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:47.240
no keywords are appearing.

00:15:48.140 --> 00:15:51.170
I wonder if this means that
there are no particular problems.

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:52.270
Meroko.

00:15:52.640 --> 00:15:53.300
Huh?

00:15:53.670 --> 00:15:55.770
Doesn't that email bother you?

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:56.800
Why?

00:15:58.070 --> 00:15:59.500
No particular reason, but...

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:04.040
He probably listened to the CD that
the teacher from the orphanage gave him.

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:08.370
Why don't you just be happy for
Mitsuki, who's doing her best?

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:16.370
Okay, I have a meeting,
so you go on ahead.

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:18.140
Yes, all right.

00:16:29.140 --> 00:16:29.800
What?

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:31.840
Huh?

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:36.340
Wasn't the dressing room up?

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:39.200
That's strange.
Anyway, let's try going down.

00:16:54.300 --> 00:16:58.200
Why won't it stop?
It keeps going up.

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:14.500
The roof?

00:17:27.800 --> 00:17:28.800
I've been waiting.

00:17:32.670 --> 00:17:33.740
W-What?

00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:35.270
What is this?

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:39.640
Ow, ow, ow...

00:17:42.900 --> 00:17:44.200
Oh no.

00:17:44.670 --> 00:17:46.940
I-It doesn't look like she's here.

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:03.970
W-What did you come here for?

00:18:05.670 --> 00:18:07.770
Everyone asks me the same thing.

00:18:09.470 --> 00:18:11.740
It's boring always giving
the same answer, so...

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:18.570
Let me see. I guess I'll say something like,
Mitsuki, I've come to take your life early.

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:22.370
B-But my life isn't over yet!

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:29.500
So I'll just take a reservation.

00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:33.900
Take the Death Spirit Seal, Mitsuki.

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:35.870
N-No!

00:18:41.240 --> 00:18:42.600
She's not here yet.

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:45.570
I really wonder where she went.

00:18:45.800 --> 00:18:46.800
<i>N-No!</i>

00:18:55.240 --> 00:18:56.500
N-No!

00:18:57.200 --> 00:19:01.040
Why? You're going to
die next spring anyway.

00:19:01.670 --> 00:19:04.870
Then it shouldn't be a problem
if we do the seal now.

00:19:06.970 --> 00:19:08.240
N-No.

00:19:12.740 --> 00:19:13.400
No!

00:19:14.070 --> 00:19:17.270
No! Eichi!
Meroko! Takuto!

00:19:18.900 --> 00:19:20.000
Let go of Mitsuki!

00:19:20.940 --> 00:19:21.940
Let go of her!

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:23.100
Takuto!

00:19:24.240 --> 00:19:25.670
Mitsuki, are you okay?!

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:29.170
Oh, it seems you've caught me.

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:34.140
You little... Don't be so rash!
We're in charge of her!

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:37.200
It's because you guys work slow.

00:19:37.340 --> 00:19:38.500
What?!

00:19:38.970 --> 00:19:42.540
After all, she's actually
getting better, isn't she?

00:19:43.270 --> 00:19:45.140
Because of Eichi's email
or something.

00:19:45.900 --> 00:19:49.100
Don't tell me...
Don't tell me that you...

00:19:50.040 --> 00:19:53.140
Insightful, master detective Mero.

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:55.840
Mitsuki!

00:19:55.870 --> 00:19:57.570
We were looking for you, Mitsuki!

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:02.340
Izumi!

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:07.540
Well, I guess that's enough for today.
See you again soon.

00:20:07.670 --> 00:20:09.170
Adios.

00:20:09.800 --> 00:20:11.170
That Izumi...

00:20:12.370 --> 00:20:14.400
Mitsuki! I have wonderful news!

00:20:14.740 --> 00:20:20.400
W-What are you so flustered about?
And what are you doing here, Dr. Wakaoji?

00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:23.540
A new method of treatment has
been discovered in America!

00:20:24.100 --> 00:20:27.170
With that method, we can operate
without harming your vocal cords.

00:20:27.570 --> 00:20:28.240
What?!

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:31.870
You'll be able to keep singing
if the surgery is a success!

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:35.340
You can keep on living, Mitsuki!

00:20:37.340 --> 00:20:39.070
Is that true?

00:20:39.740 --> 00:20:40.400
Yes!

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:45.940
Isn't that great, Mitsuki?

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:49.100
Eichi's email,
this news about my throat...

00:20:49.940 --> 00:20:51.040
I feel like so many
good things are happening

00:20:51.070 --> 00:20:52.300
that something bad
is bound to happen.

00:20:53.170 --> 00:20:54.170
Mitsuki?

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:57.470
But if something bad happens,
I'm ready for it.

00:20:57.900 --> 00:21:01.400
I feel like I'd have no problem
at all dealing with it!

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:05.440
That's the spirit, Mitsuki!
Get better and see Eichi!

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:09.440
Oh no, what was I thinking?

00:21:10.770 --> 00:21:11.440
Sorry.

00:21:15.340 --> 00:21:19.300
She doesn't know that Eichi's email
was Izumi's doing.

00:21:20.170 --> 00:21:23.440
What should we do, Takuto?
She's so happy.

00:21:23.470 --> 00:21:25.970
How do we tell her the truth?

00:23:06.040 --> 00:23:11.570
Hey, Takuto. I think we should tell her
that the email wasn't really from Eichi.

00:23:11.700 --> 00:23:14.540
No! She's so happy!

00:23:14.900 --> 00:23:17.940
Plus, she's in a contest for
the Best New Singer Award in America!

00:23:18.200 --> 00:23:22.600
I know! But isn't it crueler
to make her happy with lies?

00:23:22.940 --> 00:23:25.970
I know that too. But...

00:23:26.900 --> 00:23:30.870
Next time on Full Moon:
"The Best New Singer Award."

00:23:31.670 --> 00:23:32.670
- Look forward to it!
- Look forward to it!
